  "output": {
    "answer": "That's not something the record actually tests — everything documented is about scaling from one person to multiple model-tier lanes, not to multiple human engineers. The closest documented change: once the work outgrew one context window, the fix was a coordinating layer that writes briefs and judges, while other lanes do bounded work, and every lane needed a self-contained brief plus a provenance contract, with whoever reviews a lane's output required to be a tier stronger than whoever ran it. Whether that same structure holds up for a team of engineers sharing the same lanes and gates isn't shown in what I have here.",
